OL,2,V55555555CPOLL TAX FAIRER
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CTHAN RATES - THATCHER
OL,5, Mrs Thatcher has held firm in the face
OL,6, of rising Tory discontent by making a
OL,7, robust defence of the community charge.
OL,9, She said the poll tax was fairer than
OL,10, the rates, which made it all too easy
OL,11, for people to vote for higher spending
OL,12, while others picked up the bill.
OL,14, The Prime Minister said Labour's plans
OL,15, would not just be "a tax on roofs, but
OL,16, floors and extensions as well".
OL,18, She told Tory councillors at a London
OL,19, conference that about one in four
OL,20, people would get rebates - more than
OL,21, did so under the present system.
OL,23,F]DFrom 03-03-90 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49605
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772570817
OL,1,V7w3s7s35B                         G5/24
OL,2,V55555555CTHOUSANDS JOIN
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CPOLL TAX PROTESTS
OL,5, Thousands of demonstrators have been
OL,6, marching in Tory strongholds in South-
OL,7, West England to protest at the poll tax
OL,9, One of the biggest rallies was in
OL,10, Taunton, Somerset, where some Tory
OL,11, supporters said they would no longer
OL,12, back the party.
OL,14,SGThree hundred wooden beach hut owners
OL,15, are to receive demands for half a poll
OL,16, tax bill of #320 for their properties.
OL,18, Bournemouth council's Elspeth Raisbeck
OL,19, said they were liable to pay because
OL,20, the huts, which overlook Christchurch
OL,21, Bay, had sleeping accommodation.
OL,23,F]DFrom 03-03-90 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49606
SC,0006
